# SPEC-002 — Engineering Toolchain

**Specification ID:** SPEC-002  
**Title:** Engineering Toolchain  
**Version:** 0.1.0  
**Status:** Draft  
**Priority:** High  
**Epic:** Platform Foundation

---

# Purpose

Establish a consistent development environment that ensures code quality, repeatability, and maintainability across all contributors.

This specification focuses on engineering workflows rather than application features.

---

# Objectives

The project shall provide:

- consistent formatting
- static analysis
- type checking
- automated testing
- pre-commit validation
- continuous integration
- reproducible development environments

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- uv
- Ruff
- mypy
- pytest
- Playwright
- pre-commit
- GitHub Actions

---

## Out of Scope

- deployment
- application features
- authentication
- database
- frontend functionality

---

# Functional Requirements

## FR-001

Dependency management shall use **uv**.

---

## FR-002

Formatting and linting shall use **Ruff**.

---

## FR-003

Static type analysis shall use **mypy**.

---

## FR-004

Backend tests shall use **pytest**.

---

## FR-005

Browser tests shall use **Playwright**.

---

## FR-006

Developers shall be able to execute all quality checks using a single command.

Example:

```
make check
```

or

```
just check
```

(The implementation may choose either approach.)

---

## FR-007

GitHub Actions shall execute:

- formatting
- linting
- type checking
- unit tests

on every pull request.

---

## FR-008

Pre-commit hooks shall prevent common quality issues before commit.

---

# Non-Functional Requirements

The engineering toolchain shall:

- work on Linux
- work on macOS
- work on Windows
- work in GitHub Codespaces
- work in GitHub Actions
- work without proprietary software

---

# Acceptance Criteria

- Dependencies install successfully
- Ruff passes
- mypy passes
- pytest passes
- Playwright smoke test passes
- pre-commit executes successfully
- GitHub Actions succeeds

---

# Deliverables

- pyproject.toml
- uv.lock
- .pre-commit-config.yaml
- GitHub Actions workflow
- Playwright configuration
- Developer documentation

---

# Definition of Done

- Engineering toolchain configured
- CI pipeline green
- Local setup documented
- Contributor onboarding verified